If you press the button on his nose where the 'S' is, it'll switch to
'R' and Dusty will switch to working in reverse.

Did you pick up Dusty and press the space bar to turn him on?

Did you find the '-1' in the pile of junk?

Hmmm.  Here's what I would do.  Point to Dusty's button, click, 
point to any other part of Dusty, click, and then press the space bar. When I
see him spit out the '-1', I'd press ' ' again to turn him off.  Then
I'd pick up the -1.


